#!/bin/sh
# After each commit, note which commit took in the uncommitted work a page
# comment was made on (development-manager's page comments: `restamp` appends
# one line to that comment's thread file). It never changes the commit and
# never stops it.
#
# This is the tracked copy of the hook enable-page-comments writes into
# .git/hooks. This repo runs its hooks from .githooks (core.hooksPath), so the
# .git/hooks copy never runs here.
top=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null)
if [ -n "$top" ] && [ -x "$top/.page-comments/run" ]; then
  "$top/.page-comments/run" restamp 2>/dev/null || true
fi
exit 0
